(src/roster.vox: read the names file into a list of names, roster order.)

see textkit version "0.2" from "textkit.lib".

a list called names is [].

To 'read the names from' with a text called path.
  Open a file for reading called 'the names file' at path.
  On error print "scheduler: cannot open {path}", exit 1.
  a buffer called 'the file content'.
  Read from 'the names file' into 'the file content'.
  Close 'the names file'.
  a text called 'the file text' is 'the file content' as text.
  a list called 'the raw lines' is 'split lines' of 'the file text'.
  For each 'raw line' in 'the raw lines',
    a text called 'the trimmed line' is trim of 'raw line',
    if 'the trimmed line' is not empty then, append 'the trimmed line' to names..
  If names's length is less than 2 then,
    Print "scheduler: need at least two people in {path}",
    Exit 1.

To 'the longest name length'.
  a number called longest is 0.
  For each person in names,
    a number called 'this name length' is 'text length' of person,
    if 'this name length' is greater than longest then, the longest is 'this name length'..
  Return a number, longest.
